ized]] system, bitcoin operates without a central authority or single administrator,<ref name=Gervais2014>{{Cite journal |last1=Gervais |first1=Arthur |last2=Karame |first2=Ghassan O. |last3=Capkun |first3=Vedran |last4=Capkun |first4=Srdjan |date=May 2014 |title=Is Bitcoin a Decentralized Currency? |journal=[[IEEE Security & Privacy]] |volume=12 |issue=3 |pages=54–60 |doi=10.1109/MSP.2014.49 |bibcode=2014ISPri..12c..54G |s2cid=13948781 |issn=1540-7993 }}</ref> so that anyone can create a new bitcoin address and transact without needing any approval.{{r|Antonopoulos2014|page=ch. 1}} This is accomplished through a specialized [[distributed ledger]] called a ''[[blockchain]]'' that records bitcoin transactions.{{r|econbc}}

